package build

//
// This third meta-level exists for one reason: so that mill-build/build.mill can
// say `import untemplate.mill.UntemplateModule`.
//
// As of mill 1.1.0, there is no other way to get a dependency there.
//
//   - A `//| mvnDeps` header in mill-build/build.mill does nothing. Mill does
//     parse nested build headers -- put invalid YAML in one and it complains --
//     but only for a boolean it needs during build-file discovery. mvnDeps at
//     that level is read and discarded, with no diagnostic. The failure you get
//     is "Not found: untemplate" at the import, pointing nowhere useful.
//   - The root build.mill's `//| mvnDeps` header cannot supply it either. That
//     header *is* mill-build's mvnDeps -- not an addition to it but an override
//     of it -- so it configures the level below this one. Declare both the header
//     and a mvnDeps task in mill-build/build.mill and mill refuses outright:
//     "Build header config conflicts with task defined in mill-build/build.mill".
//
// So the header shortcut exists only for the level mill generates for you. Own
// that level, as mill-build/build.mill does, and you own its mvnDeps; to give it
// dependencies of its own, this file is the mechanism. Deleting it breaks the
// build.
//
// This is version-specific, and worth re-testing on a mill upgrade. A header in
// mill-build/build.mill worked in mill 1.0.6 -- the last 1.0.x release -- and has
// not worked in any release since. Bisected with the same four files, out/ wiped
// before each run, classified on exit status and on whether the import resolved:
//
//     1.0.6   exit 0   honored
//     1.1.0   exit 1   IGNORED
//     1.1.10  exit 1   IGNORED
//     1.3.0   exit 1   IGNORED
//
// So it is not fixed as of 1.3.0, the current release. (There is no 1.0.7 or
// 1.0.9, and no 1.2.0 final -- 1.0.6 is followed by 1.1.0-RC1, and 1.2.0 stopped
// at RC1.)
//
// 1.1.0 is where build headers were reworked, and where
// https://github.com/com-lihaoyi/mill/issues/6202 was fixed -- the mirror-image
// complaint that a *root* header was silently ignored when a meta-build existed.
// The fix established the override semantics above ("YAML overwriting its
// meta-build is the correct mental model of the status quo") and replaced that
// silent failure with the conflict error. The symmetric case, a header one level
// down, is not discussed there and silently does nothing. If that is ever made to
// work, this file and its sibling header can both go away.
//
// Two dead ends, so they need not be retried:
//
//   - mill-build/build.mill.yaml does not help. Mill treats a .mill.yaml as a
//     replacement for the .mill file, not a companion -- "Multiple root build
//     files found: build.mill.yaml,build.mill, picking build.mill.yaml" -- so it
//     cannot serve a file that needs Scala, as mill-build/build.mill does.
//   - The YAML form is irrelevant. Inline `["..."]` and a block list behave
//     identically, at every level.
//
// One trap, since the sibling unstatic projects are all pinned to 1.0.6: because
// the resolved meta-build classpath persists in out/, bumping one of them to
// 1.1.x keeps building until something clears out/, and only then fails with
// "Not found: untemplate" for no apparent reason.
//

import mill.*, scalalib.*
import mill.meta.MillBuildRootModule

object `package` extends MillBuildRootModule:

  override def mvnDeps = Seq(
    mvn"com.mchange::untemplate-mill:0.3.0",
  )
